{"text": "be qo\nLact tei\n\n1992-12-22 15136 REYNOLDS TOBACCO COLOGNE 49 221 1646 287 a2\n\nRJ. REYNOLOS TOBACCO INTERNATIONAL - COLOGNE OFFICE\nR&D - SCIENTIFIC AFFAIRS\n\nDATE: December 22, 1992\nTO: Cooper Rees ce: Wolfgang D. Dahne\nRobert L. Suber\nFROM: Lutz. Mueller\nSUBJECT: Additives Regulations in France\nPlease find attached the final version of Mme. H\u00e9l\u00e9ne Bourgols' report on the meeting of\n\nthe Working Group \"Additives on Tobsceo\" in which she participated on behalf of\nGF-CC. (the Importers' Association).\n\nBob: This final version is not really different in content from the draft version which 1 gave\n\u2018you last Friday in Winston-Salem; there is only a new arrangement of certain paragraphs.\n\nThe outcome of the meeting of the Working Group puts even more weight on two of the\nrequired activities which we discussed last week in Winston-Salem:\n\n1) We should take 2 critical look at the 1984 Ordinance in order to identify those) yy ac,\n\nadditives which should be eliminated or could be \"sacrificed\". We need to do this in order\n10 create a aound basis for the Working Group in case they really want to recommend to\nthe Ministry to re-Instate the 1984 Ordinance in revised form and keop it valid until a\nharmonized BC regulation is adopted by the EC member states,\n\n2 \u2018We should come up with recommendations concerning the volume and nature of\ndata required to demonstrate the acceptablty of a (new) additive, However, to look at\nGermany and the more recent additions to the Tobacco Ordinance will be much less\nhelpful than orginally thought for the following reasons:\n\nTo explain our own example, ic. the exemption for ethyl vaniltin glucaside, in great detail\ndoes not seem to be prudent since the our approach was probably more demanding than\nwas really necessary, and it would make a much tougher yardstick than we could possibly\naccept for a wide range of additives. Another case during the last couple of years In\nGermany was cumarin; and we may not really want to use this example. The third case in\nrecent history were the \u201chot-melt\u201d polymer glues which were submitied by the paper\n\u2018manufacturers and about which we have litte detaited information.\n\nyaw ?\n4 ine Faon',\n\ng\n&\n>\ne\nFa\na", "words": [{"text": "be", "x0": 29, "y0": 371, "x1": 46, "y1": 379, "conf": 61.0}, {"text": "qo", "x0": 54, "y0": 372, "x1": 81, "y1": 381, "conf": 21.0}, {"text": "Lact", "x0": 37, "y0": 391, "x1": 72, "y1": 398, "conf": 29.0}, {"text": "tei", "x0": 79, "y0": 389, "x1": 100, "y1": 396, "conf": 11.0}, {"text": "1992-12-22", "x0": 134, "y0": 10, "x1": 198, "y1": 18, "conf": 87.0}, {"text": "15136", "x0": 220, "y0": 10, "x1": 252, "y1": 18, "conf": 43.0}, {"text": "REYNOLDS", "x0": 272, "y0": 10, "x1": 325, "y1": 18, "conf": 67.0}, {"text": "TOBACCO", "x0": 332, "y0": 9, "x1": 378, "y1": 18, "conf": 61.0}, {"text": "COLOGNE", "x0": 385, "y0": 9, "x1": 431, "y1": 18, "conf": 90.0}, {"text": "49", "x0": 492, "y0": 9, "x1": 505, "y1": 18, "conf": 76.0}, {"text": "221", "x0": 512, "y0": 9, "x1": 531, "y1": 18, "conf": 83.0}, {"text": "1646", "x0": 540, "y0": 9, "x1": 565, "y1": 18, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "287", "x0": 572, "y0": 9, "x1": 592, "y1": 18, "conf": 54.0}, {"text": "a2", "x0": 613, "y0": 9, "x1": 626, "y1": 18, "conf": 48.0}, {"text": "RJ.", "x0": 158, "y0": 113, "x1": 184, "y1": 124, "conf": 69.0}, {"text": "REYNOLOS", "x0": 194, "y0": 112, "x1": 277, "y1": 124, "conf": 92.0}, {"text": "TOBACCO", "x0": 286, "y0": 112, "x1": 362, "y1": 125, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "INTERNATIONAL", "x0": 371, "y0": 113, "x1": 493, "y1": 125, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "-", "x0": 502, "y0": 119, "x1": 507, "y1": 122, "conf": 92.0}, {"text": "COLOGNE", "x0": 516, "y0": 113, "x1": 593, "y1": 126, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "OFFICE", "x0": 598, "y0": 114, "x1": 654, "y1": 126, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "R&D", "x0": 295, "y0": 145, "x1": 335, "y1": 157, "conf": 91.0}, {"text": "-", "x0": 344, "y0": 151, "x1":